* t43evbusy.a -- CONF68K test t43: an event cannot be deleted while its use* count is not zero.** Claim (DOCS/claims.md): "Events have an implicit use count (initially set to* one), which is incremented with each Ev$Link call and decremented with each* Ev$UnLnk call.  An event may not be deleted unless its use count is zero"* (page 1-21), which lists E$EvBusy, 169, as the error -- "The event has a* non-zero link count".** The count starts at ONE, not zero, so this needs no second process and no* Ev$Link at all: the creator itself holds the one link Ev$Creat gave it, and* a delete attempted straight afterwards must be refused.  That is the whole* test.  A system that frees the entry anyway reports 0 here.** Note what this does NOT assume.  It never asks whether some LATER delete* succeeds -- that is t44, deliberately separate, because the two halves fail* independently and the manual is self-contradictory about the second one.*Prgrm set 1Objct set 1ReEnt set $80Type_Lang set (Prgrm<<8)+ObjctAttr_Rev set (ReEnt<<8)+1FEvent set $53EvUnLnk set 1EvCreat set 2EvDelet set 3*INITVAL set 55EXPECT set 169* psect t43evbusy,Type_Lang,Attr_Rev,0,2048,startstart lea evname(pc),a0 move.l #INITVAL,d0 move.w #EvCreat,d1 move.w #0,d2 move.w #1,d3 trap #0 dc.w FEvent bcs.w setuperr move.l d0,d5** The delete this test is about.  Success is the failure: the event still has* the link its creation gave it. lea evname(pc),a0 move.w #EvDelet,d1 trap #0 dc.w FEvent bcc.s deleted moveq #0,d6 move.w d1,d6 bra.s cleanupdeleted moveq #0,d6** Clean up whatever state the run is now in.  If the delete was refused the* event is still there and needs unlinking and deleting; if it was wrongly* allowed, both of these fail harmlessly and are ignored either way, because* this test's verdict was already decided above.cleanup move.l d5,d0 move.w #EvUnLnk,d1 trap #0 dc.w FEvent lea evname(pc),a0 move.w #EvDelet,d1 trap #0 dc.w FEvent* cmpi.l #EXPECT,d6 beq.w ispass bra.w isfail* use verdict.i use report.i*evname dc.b "cf43ev",0idstr dc.b "RESULT t43 ",0passtr dc.b "PASS",0failstr dc.b "FAIL",0errstr dc.b "ERROR",0obsstr dc.b "  obs=",0expstr dc.b " exp=",0descstr dc.b "  Ev$Delet refuses an event whose use count is not zero",0 ends